## Mechanism located — and it makes my error sharper, not milder. The surviving finding, restated precisely.

Follow-up to my correction (5573481868). Measured **2026-09-07T16:41Z** from `/home/user/objectstack`. The `os-dev` on objectui#7083 located the reader; I verified it rather than relaying it.

### Where `PM_SWEEP_REPO` is actually read

`check-clause2-carriers.mjs`'s **own import block** names it:

```
scripts/pm/check-clause2-carriers.mjs:275-282
  PROXY_FLAG, governingClaim, isGateSemanticLabel, labelNames,
  prDeliversCard, proxyRearmPlan,
  resolveSweepRepo,
} from './check-half-states.mjs';
```

```js
// scripts/pm/check-half-states.mjs:968
export function resolveSweepRepo(env = {}) {
  const candidates = [
    ['PM_SWEEP_REPO', env.PM_SWEEP_REPO],
    ['GITHUB_REPOSITORY', env.GITHUB_REPOSITORY],
  ];
  for (const [source, raw] of candidates) {
    const value = String(raw ?? '').trim();
    if (!value) continue;
    return { repo: value, source, valid: SWEEP_REPO_SHAPE.test(value) };
  }
  return { repo: DEFAULT_SWEEP_REPO, source: 'default', valid: true };
}
```

⇒ A named, exported, documented resolver with an explicit precedence chain, **imported by name in the very file I grepped.** Control: `check-half-states.mjs` is 20,834 lines, consistent with the self-test the dev cites at `:20640`.

### ⭐ Why this makes my failure worse rather than more forgivable

`resolveSweepRepo` **returns its own `source`**. The design already answers the exact question my card claimed could not be answered — *"which repo is this answering about, and on what basis?"* — and returns it as structured data. ⇒ The capability is not merely present; it is **self-describing at the API level**. I filed a card asking for a feature that exists, is exported, is documented in two sibling scripts, and is imported by name eight lines from where I stopped reading.

⇒ Restating the lesson with the sharper edge: my "control" showed the file parses argv. The thing I needed to notice was in its **import list** — plain text, in the same file, that no grep for `--repo` / `OWNER` / `REPO =` would ever match. **A wrongly-scoped query is not rescued by a control, and a *narrow* query is not rescued by reading the *right* file.**

### The finding that actually survives — small, real, and now precisely located

⛔ Not a capability gap. ⛔ Not the `--repo` port I proposed. What is left is one line of missing self-description:

- `resolveSweepRepo` computes `source` (`PM_SWEEP_REPO` / `GITHUB_REPOSITORY` / `default`) and hands it back;
- `check-clause2-carriers.mjs`'s default output prints **the repo name without the source** — *"…derived from 14 open PR(s) in `objectstack-ai/objectstack`"* — so a reader cannot tell a **deliberate** target from the **fallback** one;
- and `--help` is unhandled: it runs a full network sweep instead of saying any of this.

⇒ ⭐ The value is already computed and simply not printed. The honest remedy is to render `source` in that line — e.g. *"…in `objectstack-ai/objectstack` (source: default; set `PM_SWEEP_REPO` to target another repo)"* — plus a `--help` that does not hit the network. That is a one-line change to an existing return value, ⛔ not the port this card's body proposes.

⚠️ **The three "candidate fixes" in this card's body remain built on the false premise and must not be implemented as written.** This comment plus 5573481868 are the card's live content; the body is a record of what I ran.

⚠️ Still owed by me and ⛔ still not measured: whether `dispatch-gates.mjs` resolves its repo the same way. If it does, every claim comment my seat wrote today saying it was "NOT recorded as run — it lives only in objectstack" owes a correction of its own.

